msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:137
msgid ""
"|img-match-pending-0| |img-match-pending-1| |img-match-pending-2| |img-match-"
"pending-3| |img-match-pending-4| |img-match-pending-5| (Pending)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:111
msgid "img-match-pending-0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:115
msgid "img-match-pending-1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:119
msgid "img-match-pending-2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:123
msgid "img-match-pending-3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:127
msgid "img-match-pending-4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:131
msgid "img-match-pending-5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:0
msgid ""
"These icons appear for a track that has a single matched file, and indicate "
"how closely the metadata currently assigned to the track corresponds to the "
"metadata from the matched audio file saved on disk. The fill grows and "
"shifts from red toward green as the match improves. The icons are divided "
"into six levels: a leftmost red level for a poor match, four intermediate "
"levels, and a fully green level that is shown only for an exact match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:0
msgid ""
"Because this reflects the *pending* differences between the track metadata "
"and the metadata for the audio file stored on disk, a track with unsaved "
"changes shows one of these match icons rather than the saved indicator, even "
"when the match is a perfect green. Once the file is saved (so that the "
"loaded metadata and the metadata in the audio file on disk are identical) "
"the icon changes to the saved indicator described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:0
msgid ""
"The icons are displayed dimmed (the *Pending* row above) when there is a "
"pending action for the track, such as the file being queued for saving."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:150
msgid "|img-track-saved|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:146
msgid "img-track-saved"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:0
msgid ""
"This icon indicates that the matched file has no unsaved changes: the data "
"loaded in Picard is identical to the data stored on disk (for example, right "
"after the file has been saved). This is different from a fully green match "
"icon, which marks a *perfect match that still has unsaved changes* pending."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:159
msgid "|img-error-no-access|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:155
msgid "img-error-no-access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:0
msgid ""
"This icon indicates that Picard encountered a permission error while trying "
"to load or save the file. This is typically due to the file being marked as "
"read-only, or you do not have sufficient permission to read the file or save "
"the file in the specified directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:168
msgid "|img-error-not-found|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:164
msgid "img-error-not-found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:0
msgid ""
"This icon indicates that Picard could not find the file with the given path "
"while trying to load or save the track. This is typically due to the file "
"being moved or deleted since it was loaded into Picard, but could also be "
"due to a missing directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:177
msgid "|img-dialog-error|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:173
msgid "img-dialog-error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:179
msgid ""
"This icon indicates that Picard encountered an error while trying to load or "
"save the track. This is typically due to a problem writing the tags into the "
"file, but could also be due to a storage IO error on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:183
msgid ":index:`Status Bar <icons; status bar, status bar>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:185
msgid ""
"There is a status bar at the bottom of Picard's main screen, which displays "
"some information about current processing status. This includes four numbers "
"along with the current port number that Picard is monitoring, and a "
"notification icon if there are any plugin updates available. In addition, if "
"Picard is currently processing your files an estimated time to completion "
"will also be displayed to the left of the status indicators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:190
msgid "From left to right, the numbers represent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:192
msgid ""
"The estimated processing time remaining (only displayed if Picard is "
"actively processing files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:193
msgid "The number of files loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:194
msgid "The number of MusicBrainz releases loaded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:195
msgid ""
"The number of files with pending action (e.g. loading, saving, "
"fingerprinting)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:196
msgid "The number of active network requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../getting_started/status_icons.rst:198
msgid ""
"If there are any plugin updates available and the notification icon is "
"displayed, clicking the icon will open the Plugins options page where you "
"can review the available plugin updates and select which ones to install."
msgstr ""
